        "title": "fix(inworld): use truncateUtf16Safe for error body and parse error truncation",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nTwo `.slice(0, N)` truncation sites in the Inworld TTS extension may cut UTF-16 surrogate pairs in half when the error body or parse error message contains multi-byte characters such as emoji.\n\n## Changes\n\n- `extensions/inworld/tts.ts`: replace `collapsed.slice(0, INWORLD_ERROR_BODY_MAX_CHARS)` and `trimmed.slice(0, 80)` with `truncateUtf16Safe` to keep truncated output valid Unicode.\n\nLabel: bugfix | merge-risk: 🟢 minimal",
